{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.ProtonTrefoilSign","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.ProtonTrefoilSign","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.neutron_more_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.neutron_more_negative","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L303-L317","doc":"The difference is negative for all q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trefoilDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trefoilDiff","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L292-L301","doc":"The neutron has MORE trefoil demand than the proton:\n\nc_{e⁻}(𝔫) − c_{e⁻}(𝔭) = −(q−1)⁴(q+1)⁴(q⁴+1) / (4q⁶)\n\nThis difference is always negative for q > 1, meaning the\nneutron's e⁻ coefficient is more negative than the proton's.\nThis is why the FREE NEUTRON beta-decays but the free proton\ndoes not (at our q₀). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.neutron_trefoil_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.neutron_trefoil_neg","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L269-L288","doc":"c_{e⁻}(𝔫) < 0 for all q > 1.\nProof: (q−1)² > 0, (q+1)² > 0, (q²+1)² > 0, 4q⁴ > 0.\nProduct is positive, so −product < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.neutronTrefoilCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.neutronTrefoilCoeff","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L257-L267","doc":"The neutron e⁻ coefficient is ALWAYS NEGATIVE for q > 1.\nNo sign polynomial analysis needed — the formula is a\nperfect negative square:\n\nc_{e⁻}(𝔫) = −(q−1)²(q+1)²(q²+1)² / (4q⁴)\n\nAll factors in the numerator are perfect squares (≥ 0),\nthe denominator is positive, and the overall sign is −.\nTherefore c_{e⁻}(𝔫) ≤ 0 for all q, with equality only at q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.proton_trefoil_neg_on_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.proton_trefoil_neg_on_interval","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L227-L253","doc":"The proton e⁻ coefficient is negative for all q ∈ (1, 3/2].\n\nSince q₀ ≈ 1.110 ∈ (1, 3/2], this proves the proton has\nnegative trefoil demand at the physical substrate parameter.\n\nCombined with neutron_trefoil_neg (which holds for ALL q > 1),\nboth nucleons have e⁻ < 0 — the beta decay channel is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_neg_on_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_neg_on_interval","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L197-L225","doc":"**THE KEY RESULT: p(q) < 0 for all q ∈ [1, 3/2].**\n\nDirect algebraic proof — no monotonicity or IVT needed!\n\nWrite −p(q) = 3q⁶ − q⁸ + 3q² − 1 = q⁶(3 − q²) + (3q² − 1).\n\nFor q ∈ [1, 3/2]:\n• 3 − q² ≥ 3 − 9/4 = 3/4 > 0   (since q ≤ 3/2)\n• q⁶ ≥ 1                          (since q ≥ 1)\n• 3q² − 1 ≥ 2 > 0                (since q ≥ 1)\n\nTherefore −p(q) ≥ 1 · 3/4 + 2 = 11/4 > 0, so p(q) < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_deriv_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_deriv_neg","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L184-L195","doc":"p'(q) = 2q · r(q) < 0 for q ∈ (1, 3/2].\nSince r(q) < 0 (proved above) and q > 0, the product is negative.\nTherefore p is strictly decreasing on [1, 3/2]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_neg_on_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_neg_on_interval","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L162-L182","doc":"r(q) = 4q⁶ − 9q⁴ − 3 < 0 for all q ∈ [1, 3/2].\n\nProof: write r(q) = q⁴(4q² − 9) − 3.\nFor q ≤ 3/2: 4q² ≤ 4·(9/4) = 9, so 4q² − 9 ≤ 0.\nSince q⁴ ≥ 0, we get q⁴(4q² − 9) ≤ 0.\nTherefore r(q) ≤ 0 − 3 = −3 < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_3_2_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_3_2_neg","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L158-L160","doc":"r(3/2) < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_one_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_one_neg","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L154-L156","doc":"r(1) < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_3_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_3_2","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L150-L152","doc":"r(3/2) = −3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.derivFactor_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L146-L148","doc":"r(1) = −8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.derivFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.derivFactor","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L141-L144","doc":"The derivative factor r(q) = 4q⁶ − 9q⁴ − 3.\np'(q) = 2q · r(q), so sign(p') = sign(r) for q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.proton_trefoil_neg_at_11_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.proton_trefoil_neg_at_11_10","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L122-L137","doc":"The proton e⁻ coefficient is negative for q = 11/10.\n\nSince q₀ ≈ 1.110 and p is continuous, and p(11/10) < 0\nand p(12/10) < 0, the coefficient is negative throughout\nthe interval [1.1, 1.2] which contains q₀.\n\nprotonTrefoilCoeff(11/10) = (1/10)²·(21/10)²·p(11/10)/(4·(11/10)⁶)\nThe prefactor (q−1)²(q+1)²/(4q⁶) is positive for q > 1.\nSo sign = sign(p) < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_18_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_18_10","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L113-L120","doc":"p(18/10) < 0.  Direct rational evaluation.\np(9/5) = −217604/390625 < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_15_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_15_10","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L104-L111","doc":"p(15/10) < 0.  Direct rational evaluation.\np(3/2) = −3659/256 < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_12_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_12_10","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L95-L102","doc":"p(12/10) < 0.  Direct rational evaluation.\np(6/5) = −3116459/390625 < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_11_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_11_10","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L84-L93","doc":"p(11/10) < 0.  Direct rational evaluation.\np(11/10) = (11/10)⁸ − 3(11/10)⁶ − 3(11/10)² + 1\n         = 214358881/100000000 − 3·1771561/1000000 − 3·121/100 + 1\n         = −580109419/100000000 < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.proton_trefoil_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.proton_trefoil_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L75-L82","doc":"At q = 1, the proton e⁻ coefficient is 0.\n(The (q−1)² factor vanishes.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.protonTrefoilCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.protonTrefoilCoeff","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L67-L73","doc":"The proton e⁻ coefficient as a function of q.\nThis is the EXACT Laurent polynomial from the Hecke algebra\ncomputation: B₃ · C(u,u) · C(u,d) · C(u,d).\n\nc_{e⁻}(𝔭) = (q−1)²(q+1)²(q⁸−3q⁶−3q²+1) / (4q⁶) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_two_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_two_pos","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L61-L63","doc":"p(2) > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L53-L59","doc":"p(2) = 53 > 0.  (By intermediate value, p has a root in (1,2).) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_one_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_one_neg","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L49-L51","doc":"p(1) < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L41-L47","doc":"p(1) = −4 < 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.signPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.signPoly","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ProtonTrefoilSign.lean#L31-L39","doc":"The polynomial p(q) = q⁸ − 3q⁶ − 3q² + 1 that determines\nthe sign of the proton's e⁻ NF coefficient.\n\nc_{e⁻}(proton) = (q−1)²(q+1)² · p(q) / (4q⁶)\n\nSince (q−1)²(q+1)² ≥ 0 and 4q⁶ > 0 for q > 0,\nsign(c_{e⁻}) = sign(p(q)). ","signatureChunk":0}]}